      "a": "wer:\nStudents should do it by themselves.\nC. Follow these steps to create a beautiful rangoli.\nAnswer:\nStudents should do it by themselves.\nLet us Explore (Page 131)\nDo you know what a bank account is?\nIt is a safe place to keep your money, just like you keep your money safe in a gullak.\nSuppose you get \u20b9 50 for your birthday every year. You put it into your Savings Account. After a year, the bank adds \u20b9 5 more. This is called interest on the Savings Account.\nBenefits of a Savings Account:\nMeant for saving money.\nYou can add or withdraw money anytime.\nAs a reward for saving, you earn interest.\nQuestion 1. Do you have a bank account? Yes/ No\nAnswer:\nStudents should do it by themselves.\nQuestion 2. Find out more about Fixed Deposit and Recurring Deposit. Share information on these with your class.\nAnswer:\nFixed Deposits (FDs):\nFixed Deposits are a form of fixed-income investment provided by banks and other financial institutions. In an FD, a lump sum of money is placed for a set duration, and the bank offers a fixed rate of interest for that entire period. Both the interest rate and the maturity date are decided in advance. This makes FDs a safe and reliable option for growing one\u2019s savings.\nRecurring Deposits (RDs):\nA Recurring Deposit is a type of time deposit in which a fixed amount of money is deposited at regular intervals, usually every month, for a chosen tenure. It is a widely used savings method that encourages people to save regularly while earning interest on each deposit.\nLet us Observe (Page 132)\nLook at the following pictures. Can you locate them in this textbook and write their name in the space given below?\nAnswer:\nDrone\nCloth Hand Fan\nLotus\nButterfly\nBangles\nAeroplane\nSpectacles\nLantern\nSunflower\nCrutches\nCock\nGilli\nStarfish\nSpinning top\nCompass\nLaddu\nUnderstanding Class 5 English Chapter 10: Glass Bangles\nLearning about\nGlass Bangles\nin the NCERT Class 5 English Chapter 10 helps students appreciate India\u2019s vibrant culture and tradition. Practice the exercises from the\n2026-27 NCERT solutions\nand explore how creativity and heritage come together in every lesson.\nBy engaging with\nchapter-wise solutions\n, students build strong language skills and understand grammar concepts like the past perfect tense. Focus on direct questions and\nactive learning\nto perform well in examinations and develop confidence in English.\nReviewing the\nClass 5 English Glass Bangles exercises\nregularly boosts your comprehension and writing abilities. Stay organized, revise new words, and make good use of practice activities for better\nexam scores\nand overall understanding."
